{
  "_comment": "Dated, accountable ratchet for two-organisation coverage. Each entry under 'accepted_uncovered' is a NON-startup route family that reads organisation data yet has no family-targeted two-organisation test today. An entry names the family, the brief (T-<area>-<n>) that will add its test, and the expiry date by which that test must exist. The gate requires the measured set of non-startup uncovered families to EQUAL the set of still-valid (not past expiry) accepted families: a family past its expiry fails naming family, brief and date; a newly uncovered family with no entry fails; a family that gained coverage must have its entry removed (the set can only shrink, never grow silently). Startup families (account, admin connectors, intelligence, applications, admin billing, admin team, dashboard) must always be 0 uncovered and can NEVER be excused by an entry. The Investment Analysis cross-organisation leak surfaces here as the vendor_analysis and advanced_tco families, time-boxed to T-qa-22.",
